{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1016/j.molcel.2019.07.008\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"31398324","source":"MED","pmid":"31398324","pmcid":"PMC6698059","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC6698059"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.molcel.2019.07.008","title":"Reaction Mechanisms of Pol IV, RDR2, and DCL3 Drive RNA Channeling in the siRNA-Directed DNA Methylation Pathway.","authorString":"Singh J, Mishra V, Wang F, Wang F, Huang HY, Pikaard CS.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Singh J","lastName":"Singh","firstName":"Jasleen","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Mishra V","lastName":"Mishra","firstName":"Vibhor","initials":"V","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4846-4790"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA; Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang F","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Feng","initials":"F","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6324-9135"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA; Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang F","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Feng","initials":"F","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4760-8211"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA; Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Huang HY","lastName":"Huang","firstName":"Hsiao-Yun","initials":"HY","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Pikaard CS","lastName":"Pikaard","firstName":"Craig S","initials":"CS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA; Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA. Electronic address: cpikaard@indiana.edu."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6324-9135"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4760-8211"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4846-4790"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"75","journalIssueId":2847540,"dateOfPublication":"2019 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2019,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Cell","title":"Molecular cell","essn":"1097-4164","issn":"1097-2765","isoabbreviation":"Mol Cell","nlmid":"9802571"},"printPublicationDate":"2019-08-01"},"pubYear":"2019","pageInfo":"576-589.e5","abstractText":"In eukaryotes with multiple small RNA pathways, the mechanisms that channel RNAs within specific pathways are unclear. Here, we reveal the reactions that account for channeling in the small interfering RNA (siRNA) biogenesis phase of the Arabidopsis RNA-directed DNA methylation pathway. The process begins with template DNA transcription by NUCLEAR RNA POLYMERASE IV (Pol IV), whose atypical termination mechanism, induced by nontemplate DNA base-pairing, channels transcripts to the associated RNA-dependent RNA polymerase RDR2. RDR2 converts Pol IV transcripts into double-stranded RNAs and then typically adds an extra untemplated 3' terminal nucleotide to the second strands. The dicer endonuclease DCL3 cuts resulting duplexes to generate 24- and 23-nt siRNAs. The 23-nt RNAs bear the untemplated terminal nucleotide of the RDR2 strand and are underrepresented among ARGONAUTE4-associated siRNAs. Collectively, our results provide mechanistic insights into Pol IV termination, Pol IV-RDR2 coupling, and RNA channeling, from template DNA transcription to siRNA strand discrimination.","affiliation":"Department of Biology and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biochemistry, Indiana University, Bloomington, IN 47405, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"F32 GM125334","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"R01 GM077590","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Arabidopsis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ribonuclease III","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA-Directed RNA Polymerases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Arabidopsis Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"RNA, Small Interfering","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbr